stdout | Search Erlang code by syntax-tree shape (not text) using SSR (Structural Search and Replace)
stdout | patterns.
stdout |
stdout | Usage: elp search [OPTIONS] <SSR_SPECS>...
stdout |
stdout | Arguments:
stdout |   <SSR_SPECS>...  SSR specs to use. Each accepts `PATTERN`, `ssr: PATTERN.`, or `LABEL:ssr:
stdout |                   PATTERN.` forms; the LABEL surfaces as `patternLabel` in JSON output
stdout |
stdout | Options:
stdout |       --project <PROJECT>      Path to directory with project, or to a JSON file [default: .]
stdout |       --module <MODULE>        Parse a single module from the project, not the entire project
stdout |       --app <APP>              Parse a single application from the project, not the entire project
stdout |       --file <FILE>            Parse a single file from the project, not the entire project. This
stdout |                                can be an include file or escript, etc
stdout |       --rebar                  Run with rebar
stdout |       --as <PROFILE>           Rebar3 profile to pickup [default: test]
stdout |       --include-generated      Also generate diagnostics for generated files
stdout |       --include-tests          Deprecated: has no effect, will be removed in future
stdout |       --format <FORMAT>        Customize the output format (defaults to human-readable) [possible
stdout |                                values: json]
stdout |       --macros <STRATEGY>      Macro expansion strategy (default: expand) [possible values: expand,
stdout |                                no-expand, visible-expand]
stdout |       --parens                 Explicitly match parentheses. If omitted, they are ignored
stdout |       --dump-config            Dump a configuration snippet that can be put in .elp_lint.toml to
stdout |                                match the given SSR patterns
stdout |       --show-source            Show source code context for matches
stdout |   -B, --before-context <NUM>   Print NUM lines of leading context, enables --show-source
stdout |   -A, --after-context <NUM>    Print NUM lines of trailing context, enables --show-source
stdout |   -C, --context <NUM>          Print NUM lines of output context, enables --show-source
stdout |       --group-separator <SEP>  Print SEP on line between matches with context, enables --show-source
stdout |       --no-group-separator     Do not print separator for matches with context, enables
stdout |                                --show-source
stdout |       --report-system-stats    Report system memory usage and other statistics
stdout |   -h, --help                   Print help
stdout |
stdout | Global options:
stdout |       --log-file <LOG_FILE>  
stdout |       --erl <ERL>            
stdout |       --escript <ESCRIPT>    
stdout |       --no-log-buffering     
stdout |       --no-buck-generated    Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --buck-quick-start     Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --color <WHEN>         Use color in output [default: always] [possible values: always, never,
stdout |                              auto]
stdout |
stdout | Patterns are Erlang code with placeholders:
stdout |     _@Name   match any single expression or pattern; reuse a name to require the two matches be
stdout |     equal
stdout |     _@_      anonymous wildcard (match anything, bind nothing)
stdout |     _@@Name  glob: match zero or more sibling elements (at most one glob per sequence)
stdout |
stdout | Constrain placeholders with a `where` clause, e.g. `_@X where is_atom(_@X)`.
stdout |
stdout | Examples:
stdout |     elp search 'lists:reverse(lists:reverse(_@List))'
stdout |     elp search 'case _@Cond of true -> _@Body; false -> _@Body end'
stdout |     elp search --format json 'foo(_@@Args)'
stdout |
stdout | A bare PATTERN is shorthand for `ssr: PATTERN.`. Prefix with `LABEL:ssr: ` to tag matches.
stdout |
stdout | Full syntax guide: https://whatsapp.github.io/erlang-language-platform/docs/structural-search
